  "reason": "Evidence: Our best result is config_006 (scvi_n200, multi-profile, transformer, RNA-only) at 0.653 acc, and image-only resnet50 (config_010) is very weak at 0.208. The critical open question is whether adding an image modality to the strong RNA pipeline helps or hurts. Question: config_032 (scvi_n200, multi-profile, resnet50, transformer, concat) differs from config_006 only by the addition of resnet50 with concat fusion, cleanly isolating the effect of multimodal fusion. Why this is the best next experiment: It directly tests whether multimodal fusion adds value over our best RNA-only baseline. If it improves on 0.653, we know to invest in stronger image encoders (ViT-L) and fusion strategies. If it does not, we learn that resnet50 is too weak to contribute and should pivot to testing ViT-L (config_013/014/015) before committing further budget to multimodal. This single experiment resolves the highest-uncertainty design decision (is multimodal worth pursuing?) with a minimal, interpretable change from our strongest configuration."
}

